course: dictionary
lesson: 2945
title: Dried: when the water is taken away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dried is the past form of the verb dry. When you dry something, you take the water or the wetness away. Dry, dries, dried and drying all come from the same idea.
explain: The words around a word are its context, and they give clues. «a small cake with "EAT ME" marked in currants (small dried grapes)» The brackets tell you that currants are small dried grapes, so dried means grapes that have had their water taken out.
explain: Try the swap test. «in dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud until the rain comes back.» A pool with no water left is a pool with no water in it, so dried-up means no longer having water. Your meaning fits the sentence, so it is right.
fact: Dried means made dry by taking away water or wetness.
fact: «Dried fruit» is fruit with the water taken out, so it keeps for a long time in the cupboard.
fact: «Dried up» can mean a river or pool has no water left, or that a person has no more ideas or words.
fact: Dry is the verb, and dried is its past form: dry, dries, dried, drying.
fact: Salt water left to dry leaves the salt behind, which is a way to separate a mixture.
exercise: In the sentence «a small cake with "EAT ME" marked in currants (small dried grapes)», what does dried mean? | Cooked in a hot pan | Freshly picked from the vine | *Made dry, with the water taken out | Wet and shiny
exercise: In the sentence «in dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud», what does dried-up mean? | Very noisy and busy | *No longer having water | Full to the top with water | Frozen solid in winter
exercise: Sam says dried fruit is fresh fruit with extra juice. What is the right meaning of dried fruit? | Fruit that is sold only in summer | *Fruit with the water taken out, so it keeps a long time | Fruit that is wet and sticky | Fruit that has just been picked
test: «Mopane worms are dried, stored for months and are an important food.» Why are they dried? | *To keep them for a long time | To make them fly | To make them wet and soft | To make them grow bigger
test: Which word is the past form of dry? | *dried | drying | dries | dry
exam: In the sentence «Dried tardigrades survive great cold, high pressure and radiation», what does dried mean? | Frozen in ice | *Made dry, with the water taken out | Very large and heavy | Covered in water
